<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Muslim League of Eritrea</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1946">1946</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/all-india-muslim-league">Muslim League</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eritrea">Eritrea</a> was a political party founded in 1946 by Ibrahim <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> Ali during the British administration of Eritrea. Drawing support mainly from Muslim lowlanders and opposing the Unionists who sought union with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopia">Ethiopia</a>, it campaigned for Eritrean independence and later took part in the Independence Bloc.</p></div>
